  "ingredients": [
    "2.5 pounds russet potatoes, peeled",
    "1 cup vegetable oil for frying",
    "1 cup all-purpose flour",
    "1 teaspoon garlic salt",
    "1 teaspoon onion salt",
    "1 teaspoon paprika",
    "1 teaspoon salt",
    "0.5 cup water, or as needed"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Slice potatoes into French fries; place into a large bowl of cold water to prevent them from turning brown.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/vCTvl0GKhJ81fQbLGO6QpFz_IPo=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/50223-homemade-crispy-seasoned-french-fries-ddmfs-step1-0698-d981d01988f240d181e40d58a7bd4d18.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/50223/step_01.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Heat oil in a heavy saucepan or large skillet to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": []
    },
    {
      "text": "While the oil is heating, sift flour, garlic salt, onion salt, paprika, and salt into a large bowl. Gradually stir in enough water to make a slightly thick batter that can be drizzled from a spoon.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/aoEGVo8_kzJsDtbWl0mGc0wPi2s=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/50223-homemade-crispy-seasoned-french-fries-ddmfs-step3-0702-ff3574f0bafb4f38958d58d0eb6cf3b7.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/50223/step_03.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Drain fries and pat dry; dip into batter one at a time.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/XqskpqhVvrFD5mgrugwZgDJBvec=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/50223-homemade-crispy-seasoned-french-fries-ddmfs-step4-0703-4750dda331fc4f4c9db11af2a8f64860.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/50223/step_04.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Lower fries carefully into the hot oil in batches to prevent them from clumping together; fry until golden brown and crispy on all sides, 7 to 10 minutes.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/y8aAL-RawEHvuKnWYnKQWs01B7U=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/50223-homemade-crispy-seasoned-french-fries-ddmfs-step5-0704-dd5418b73df443a4a768b6731b39342e.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/50223/step_05.webp"
    },
    {
      "text": "Drain fries on a paper towel-lined plate.",
      "section": null,
      "name": null,
      "url": null,
      "image_sources": [
        "https://www.allrecipes.com/thmb/hfspa4QYxEVVTjhiMxj86QTo-cA=/1500x0/filters:no_upscale():max_bytes(150000):strip_icc()/50223-homemade-crispy-seasoned-french-fries-ddmfs-step6-0706-4eaa284d1d5040bcb14181cecc49ef13.jpg"
      ],
      "image": "assets/images/50223/step_06.webp"
